  "slug": "safety-incident-evaluation-form",
  "title": "Safety Incident Evaluation Form",
  "subtitle": "Use this evaluation to apply explicit criteria to traceable evidence, calibrate the conclusion, authorize action, and preserve limitations for a safety incident workflow.",
  "description": "An original operational safety incident evaluation form that controls a workplace safety event and corrective-action record from identity and routing through evidence, qualified decision, exception management, implementation, handoff, and final verification.",
  "use_case": "Use when the reporting worker, supervisor, or incident coordinator needs a traceable evaluation so the qualified safety, occupational health, operations, or regulatory reviewer can stabilize, investigate, classify, notify, correct, reopen work, or escalate the safety event under the emergency procedure, hazard-control plan, incident-investigation process, reporting rules, and anti-retaliation policy without relying on an informal email, spreadsheet, or unreviewed narrative.",
  "risk_tier": "C",
